  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tri-National Response for Dignified, Peaceful and Inclusive Human Mobility in the North Countries of Central America</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This tri-national response for dignified, peaceful and inclusive human mobility in the northern countries of Central America is a project implemented by IOM, UNDP and UNHCR that aims to strengthen the capacities of the Government and civil society in El Salvador to improve the approach to the peacebuilding challenges in the context of human mobility and migration in the subregion. The project focuses on strengthening local institutions, mechanisms and coordination between key stakeholders to address and ensure the provision of better services of protection, assistance and reintegration to individuals of mixed migration flows including returnees, migrants in transit, and persons in need of international protection.</narrative>
  </description>
